Found by the k17 job 3 worker (2026-11-13). Since k17 job 3, 'in' on a SafeString checks its own keys (val, length); JS's in also walks the prototype chain, so 'toString' in m() is true (SafeString's prototype chain reaches String.prototype). Before job 3 the port threw. ADR 0014 decides own-key exists for context lookup, not for the in operator on objects -- check whether an ADR covers in; probe with the oracle.
